WEBVTT

00:19.250 --> 00:21.650
<i>For centuries the sacred magic</i>
<i>of the Divine Crystal...</i>

00:21.780 --> 00:24.190
<i>...blessed our world and its people.</i>

00:30.090 --> 00:34.200
<i>But in time the promise of its power</i>
<i>brought war to our lands.</i>

00:40.170 --> 00:45.540
<i>Lucis, a peaceful kingdom of great magic</i>
<i>kept safe by the power of the crystal.</i>

00:47.580 --> 00:51.180
<i>And Niflheim,</i>
<i>a military empire of vast machinery...</i>

00:51.310 --> 00:53.820
<i>...made strong by</i>
<i>the might of its Magitek.</i>

00:54.420 --> 00:57.250
<i>Long has war raged between the two.</i>

01:00.590 --> 01:04.090
<i>As the years passed,</i>
<i>Niflheim marched on nearby nations...</i>

01:04.260 --> 01:06.300
<i>...driven by its unsurpassed technology.</i>

01:09.130 --> 01:12.830
<i>To defend itself,</i>
<i>Lucis raised a magical wall...</i>

01:13.240 --> 01:16.240
<i>...the strength of which comes</i>
<i>from the crystal itself.</i>

01:18.140 --> 01:22.080
<i>Insomnia alone, the crown city</i>
<i>and last bastion of Lucian defense...</i>

01:22.240 --> 01:25.150
<i>...remained beyond Niflheim reach</i>
<i>for many years.</i>

01:28.780 --> 01:30.550
<i>Amid the escalating war...</i>

01:30.690 --> 01:33.260
<i>...Prince Noctis of Lucis</i>
<i>had come to Tenebrae...</i>

01:33.390 --> 01:35.660
<i>...to seek healing for a grievous injury.</i>

01:36.190 --> 01:40.330
<i>He made the long journey</i>
<i>together with his father, King Regis.</i>

01:41.430 --> 01:44.270
<i>Mother, brother, and I,</i>
<i>the royalty of Tenebrae...</i>

01:44.400 --> 01:46.400
<i>...had all welcomed their visit.</i>

02:01.320 --> 02:04.850
<i>It was then that the fires came,</i>
<i>everywhere and all at once.</i>

02:07.190 --> 02:11.460
<i>In a mere instant,</i>
<i>the whole of Tenebrae was ablaze.</i>

02:13.160 --> 02:14.860
Ravus!

02:23.510 --> 02:25.370
Mother!

02:34.750 --> 02:36.590
General Glauca.

02:43.230 --> 02:47.400
<i>The Niflheim attack was an attempt</i>
<i>on the lives of the visiting Lucian royalty.</i>

02:52.900 --> 02:54.800
Noctis!

02:59.540 --> 03:01.510
Please. Help us!

03:01.640 --> 03:03.210
King Regis!

03:17.430 --> 03:18.790
Lunafreya....

03:24.200 --> 03:25.870
Luna!

03:27.270 --> 03:28.970
<i>From that day until this day...</i>

03:29.700 --> 03:32.640
<i>...Tenebrae has been gripped</i>
<i>in the iron fist of Niflheim...</i>

03:33.480 --> 03:35.810
<i>...sworn enemy of Lucis.</i>

03:40.650 --> 03:44.890
<i>King Regis assembles a force of mighty</i>
<i>warriors to combat the imperial menace.</i>

03:45.420 --> 03:49.560
<i>Dubbed the Kingsglaive,</i>
<i>they fight relentlessly against Niflheim...</i>

03:49.690 --> 03:51.760
<i>...empowered by the magic</i>
<i>of their sovereign.</i>

04:05.940 --> 04:07.780
All units, move to secure the Wall.

04:07.910 --> 04:09.610
If they break through, we're done.

04:38.640 --> 04:40.280
What's the hold-up, Crowe?

04:40.680 --> 04:42.680
<i>Crowe! Status?</i>

04:42.980 --> 04:43.980
Almost there.

04:47.050 --> 04:48.050
No!

04:52.790 --> 04:56.460
<i>I need help. East wall's going down.</i>
<i>Pelna, can you get to me?</i>

04:57.790 --> 05:00.000
Lucis isn't paying us refugees enough...

05:01.030 --> 05:02.300
...for this.

05:18.380 --> 05:19.380
How is this fair?

05:26.090 --> 05:27.790
Nyx, I owe you one.

05:27.960 --> 05:28.990
You and everyone else.

05:29.320 --> 05:31.730
<i>We need support on the east flank.</i>
<i>Nyx, where are you?</i>

05:31.860 --> 05:32.930
I'm on my way.

05:33.060 --> 05:35.500
Pelna, fall back
and regroup with the others.

05:36.530 --> 05:37.800
Go easy on the magic, hero.

05:37.930 --> 05:39.800
You got people
waiting for you back home.

05:39.940 --> 05:41.370
I'm worth the wait.

05:43.770 --> 05:44.770
Show-off.

05:56.590 --> 05:59.520
<i>Watch your back, Libertus.</i>
<i>We got more incoming.</i>

06:00.820 --> 06:02.660
We ain't gonna last much longer.

06:05.660 --> 06:07.000
Crowe!

06:09.100 --> 06:10.100
Yes!

06:15.940 --> 06:19.670
<i>All Glaives, fall back.</i>
<i>Repeat, all Glaives fall back!</i>

07:05.890 --> 07:07.560
Release the daemon.

08:30.110 --> 08:33.940
<i>We can't take down that daemon.</i>
<i>I'm ordering a full retreat.</i>

08:34.840 --> 08:37.510
<i>Get back here alive.</i>
<i>That's an order.</i>

08:38.110 --> 08:39.180
<i>For hearth and home.</i>

08:54.560 --> 08:58.700
<i>All units, fall back to the extraction point.</i>
<i>Support is inbound.</i>

09:02.100 --> 09:04.310
Nyx! We have to get out of here.

09:05.640 --> 09:09.110
-Nyx! We have orders!
-Yeah.

09:09.240 --> 09:10.250
Help!

09:10.580 --> 09:11.580
Nyx!

09:11.810 --> 09:13.050
That idiot.

09:21.020 --> 09:22.820
Crowe. We gotta move.

09:24.860 --> 09:25.960
You gotta be kidding me.

09:59.330 --> 10:01.660
You know I ain't got
the stomach for this crap.

10:03.770 --> 10:04.900
Would you rather walk?

10:05.030 --> 10:07.040
Come on.
Just like Galahd Canyon back home.

10:20.350 --> 10:21.680
Libertus!

10:43.400 --> 10:45.640
Luche, report.

10:47.040 --> 10:50.410
The imperial forces
look to be withdrawing, sir.

11:09.160 --> 11:10.800
Guess I owe you another one.

11:11.400 --> 11:13.100
I'll put it on your tab.

11:13.370 --> 11:15.400
You just try and get some rest, all right?

11:31.750 --> 11:33.960
You disobeyed a direct order to retreat.

11:34.320 --> 11:36.020
For hearth and home, right, sir?

11:37.230 --> 11:41.930
As long as I got strength in my body,
I obey that order.

11:42.730 --> 11:44.900
Don't fool yourself, Nyx Ulric.

11:45.230 --> 11:48.270
Whatever strength you have
is on loan from the king.

11:48.740 --> 11:50.270
You are nothing without him.

11:52.110 --> 11:54.110
Await details of your reassignment.

13:02.280 --> 13:03.310
Yes, Your Majesty.

13:03.480 --> 13:05.980
Despite their victory all but assured.

13:07.850 --> 13:10.990
A sudden and inexplicable retreat.

13:11.420 --> 13:13.790
We are at risk nonetheless, Your Majesty.

13:14.290 --> 13:16.560
We cannot know
when they will strike again.

13:17.130 --> 13:19.430
Your Majesty, word from the West Gate.

13:19.790 --> 13:22.460
A man claiming to be an envoy
of the empire requests an audience.

13:26.570 --> 13:30.410
The envoy from Niflheim awaits without,
Your Majesty.

13:35.510 --> 13:36.880
Hello there.

13:37.580 --> 13:39.110
Hello!

13:39.250 --> 13:40.450
Good day to you...

13:41.120 --> 13:42.120
...and you.

13:43.280 --> 13:45.250
Well met, my dear Lucians.

13:45.420 --> 13:48.220
Has Niflheim grown so bold...

13:48.390 --> 13:51.590
...that they send the chancellor himself
as envoy?

13:52.090 --> 13:54.200
And under no guard, at that?

13:54.330 --> 13:58.370
It is an honor to be recognized
by the great King Regis.

13:58.530 --> 14:03.300
Yet permit me to stand on ceremony
and introduce myself nonetheless.

14:04.210 --> 14:08.340
Ardyn Izunia, Chancellor of Niflheim...

14:09.880 --> 14:12.380
...at your humble service.

14:12.880 --> 14:14.580
And I come to you on this...

14:14.950 --> 14:19.320
...most auspicious of days
to offer terms of peace.

14:20.220 --> 14:21.290
Peace?

14:21.860 --> 14:23.990
As you no doubt surmised...

14:24.130 --> 14:28.500
...that recent maneuver of ours
was no strategic retreat.

14:29.330 --> 14:31.000
Call it...

14:32.000 --> 14:34.970
...a gesture of imperial goodwill.

14:35.570 --> 14:37.940
Like you, we wish nothing more...

14:38.070 --> 14:42.880
...than to bring a swift end
to this senseless war.

14:43.480 --> 14:44.950
Is that so?

14:45.110 --> 14:46.110
It is, indeed.

14:46.250 --> 14:49.420
And we require
but a singular compliance.

14:49.880 --> 14:54.020
Save your grand Insomnia here.

14:54.190 --> 14:59.590
Lucis must forfeit
all territories to Niflheim rule.

15:03.130 --> 15:04.400
Insomnia!

15:04.530 --> 15:08.340
The jewel in the crown
of the Lucian kingdom.

15:09.500 --> 15:11.310
How foolish of me to forget.

15:11.470 --> 15:14.610
There is just one more trivial thing.

15:15.980 --> 15:17.250
It concerns your son.

15:19.480 --> 15:22.350
The fetching Prince Noctis of Lucis...

15:22.520 --> 15:26.250
...and the fair Princess Lunafreya
of Tenebrae....

15:27.660 --> 15:29.560
They are to be wed.

15:31.130 --> 15:33.290
You seem vexed, Your Highness.

15:34.160 --> 15:39.700
I assure you, the princess
still holds you in the highest regard...

15:40.030 --> 15:43.340
...as she has done
all these 12 long years.

16:00.320 --> 16:01.420
Don't know if anyone's told you...

16:01.560 --> 16:04.360
...but we don't take kindly
to insubordination around here.

16:08.000 --> 16:11.070
Do yourself a favor, take a look around.

16:11.500 --> 16:16.140
This is what a hundred years of peace
looks like.

16:18.710 --> 16:24.510
It's a lasting peace made by the Wall
and the Wall alone.

16:26.980 --> 16:30.620
See, we don't need any of you
immigrants...

16:31.120 --> 16:35.320
...jumping around, playing war hero.

17:08.560 --> 17:11.390
Hey!
Rough day on the gate, huh, Glaive?

17:12.090 --> 17:14.430
You jerk.
It's your fault he got stuck there.

17:16.330 --> 17:20.500
-Not a very nice welcome for a big hero.
-Not a very nice outfit for one, either.

17:20.640 --> 17:22.340
I think it brings out my eyes.

17:25.770 --> 17:27.140
What'd you put in this?

17:27.280 --> 17:28.540
Tastes like a chocobo turd.

17:28.680 --> 17:30.040
Hey, shut your trap!

17:30.480 --> 17:33.280
This ain't Galahd.
That's the way folks around here like it.

17:33.410 --> 17:38.290
Oh, well. I'm glad to see you're willing to
sell out our heritage for a few extra gil.

17:38.750 --> 17:41.520
Hey, Libertus.
You thank Nyx for saving your life yet?

17:41.660 --> 17:44.790
Oh, come on, Crowe.
Nyx and I are too close for that.

17:45.130 --> 17:47.630
He helps me, I help him.
That's the way it's always been.

17:47.760 --> 17:50.400
Looks like you got a little help
from something else, huh?

17:50.530 --> 17:52.170
I need all I can get.

17:53.330 --> 17:54.340
For hearth!

17:55.600 --> 17:56.640
-And home.
-And home.

17:59.240 --> 18:03.310
So, Nyx the Gatekeeper.
How's the new post treating you?

18:03.480 --> 18:05.480
Oh, it's amazing.
You guys would love it.

18:05.680 --> 18:07.620
The gate watch are real sweethearts.

18:08.450 --> 18:09.550
Yeah, right.

18:09.680 --> 18:12.350
We all know they hate us outsiders
more than anything.

18:12.490 --> 18:14.620
So bored they got nothing better to do.

18:14.820 --> 18:16.390
Boredom's not so bad.

18:16.520 --> 18:17.830
Means there's peace, at least.

18:18.230 --> 18:21.100
I'd fight a hundred more wars
for Galahdans to know boredom.

18:21.630 --> 18:22.800
Fight all you want.

18:23.130 --> 18:24.400
Just don't go dying yet.

18:25.170 --> 18:26.230
I still owe you.

18:26.700 --> 18:27.700
A lot.

18:27.870 --> 18:30.540
Where would the Glaive be
without its hero?

18:30.670 --> 18:33.470
Can you not talk like this
while we're drinking, please?

18:33.610 --> 18:36.740
We just sent the Niffs running
with tails between their legs, right?

18:36.880 --> 18:39.680
They weren't running from us.
No, they were toying with us.

18:41.620 --> 18:45.220
Stop being such a buzzkill, Luche.
We all know what happened.

18:45.420 --> 18:48.160
Did you know they sent an envoy
to the Citadel after that?

18:48.290 --> 18:50.690
What for? To offer their surrender?

18:50.830 --> 18:52.290
-More like demand ours.
-What?

18:52.430 --> 18:54.430
Demand? My ass!

18:54.760 --> 18:56.430
No? Think about it.

18:56.760 --> 18:58.700
The empire's got Lucis on its last legs.

18:58.830 --> 19:01.140
It's the perfect time to make demands.

19:02.740 --> 19:05.710
We are losing this war, Your Majesty.

19:06.340 --> 19:09.380
Lucis cannot rely
on the Kingsglaive alone.

19:09.510 --> 19:12.610
Accepting the truce may be
our best course of action.

19:13.150 --> 19:15.380
You speak of matters
beyond the New Wall.

19:15.650 --> 19:19.390
We have no need of a truce here,
so long as it stands.

19:19.720 --> 19:23.890
And if our position worsens,
we still have the Old Wall.

19:24.260 --> 19:29.260
Yes, but this truce
will end the fighting altogether.

19:30.360 --> 19:32.430
If only we could compromise--

19:32.570 --> 19:34.500
Compromise is unwise.

19:34.640 --> 19:37.510
We know nothing
of Niflheim's true intentions.

19:38.270 --> 19:41.810
Do not fool yourselves.
The Walls are far from impenetrable.

19:42.340 --> 19:45.380
The paths left to us are few.

19:46.350 --> 19:48.680
The New Wall draws its power
from the throne.

19:48.880 --> 19:53.720
I am able to sustain it for some years yet,
if the kingdom requires it.

19:54.960 --> 19:59.930
But the chancellor spoke one truth,
if only one.

20:00.860 --> 20:04.230
We are old, and the Old Wall....

20:05.630 --> 20:09.440
I cannot command the Old Wall
with a weakened hand...

20:09.770 --> 20:13.910
...nor do I have the strength to muster
an offensive to turn the tide on this war.

20:14.580 --> 20:16.840
Then let the choice be made,
Your Majesty.

20:17.810 --> 20:19.880
What are we to protect?

20:43.000 --> 20:44.440
<i>Help Mother!</i>

21:03.360 --> 21:05.990
How come you never
lose your lunch like that?

21:07.860 --> 21:08.900
Just doesn't add up.

21:09.330 --> 21:12.470
Here's this ancient art,
secret of the royal family and all that.

21:12.900 --> 21:14.900
Libertus! Nyx!

21:15.800 --> 21:17.540
Come here, guys, you gotta see this.

21:18.710 --> 21:20.340
<i>Things were hectic in the capital today...</i>

21:20.470 --> 21:22.280
<i>...as the Lucian government</i>
<i>announced full acceptance...</i>

21:22.410 --> 21:25.280
<i>...of what some are criticizing</i>
<i>as the unilateral peace terms...</i>

21:25.410 --> 21:27.450
<i>...proposed by Chancellor Izunia</i>
<i>of Niflheim.</i>

21:27.620 --> 21:30.820
<i>The signing of the truce will see</i>
<i>power over all Lucian territories...</i>

21:30.950 --> 21:34.360
<i>...transferred to the empire,</i>
<i>with the sole exception of Insomnia.</i>

21:34.490 --> 21:38.790
<i>In return, Niflheim guarantees</i>
<i>the safety of Insomnia and its citizenry...</i>

21:38.960 --> 21:41.300
<i>...as well as a cessation</i>
<i>to all hostilities...</i>

21:41.430 --> 21:44.370
<i>...bringing a decisive end</i>
<i>to this long and bitter war.</i>

21:47.070 --> 21:51.870
All that fighting we did.
All for nothing.

21:52.670 --> 21:55.980
Glaives.
Assemble in the briefing room.

21:57.380 --> 21:58.510
Now.

22:05.090 --> 22:07.920
The king has spoken,
and you have heard.

22:08.560 --> 22:11.690
All lands beyond the Wall
are to be relinquished to the empire.

22:11.860 --> 22:13.760
Will no regions be spared?

22:14.460 --> 22:16.760
-None.
-But your home's out there too!

22:17.060 --> 22:18.070
It is.

22:18.430 --> 22:19.930
Why would the king do this?

22:20.430 --> 22:21.900
Because it'll end this damn war.

22:24.100 --> 22:25.540
-Crowe.
-Sir!

22:26.070 --> 22:29.810
Prepare to deploy.
You're being sent to infiltrate Tenebrae.

22:30.480 --> 22:31.550
Tenebrae, sir?

22:32.350 --> 22:34.080
Mission details are classified.

22:34.620 --> 22:36.880
Report to my office for briefing
in 30 minutes.

22:38.050 --> 22:39.550
And, Nyx....

22:40.090 --> 22:41.520
You're off the West Gate.

22:41.790 --> 22:44.460
You've been reassigned
to the castle guard.

22:45.460 --> 22:46.660
That is all.

22:53.670 --> 22:56.900
So this is what you were
talking about, Luche?

22:57.070 --> 22:58.110
You heard the captain.

22:58.440 --> 23:01.580
-This wasn't our decision to make.
-Not ours to make?

23:01.740 --> 23:04.380
Those are our homes out there!
Our people!

23:04.580 --> 23:06.880
You're just gonna go along
and abandon them?

23:07.010 --> 23:08.650
If we don't go along with them...

23:08.780 --> 23:10.990
...the empire will unleash all hell
on Insomnia.

23:11.120 --> 23:13.620
-We'll unleash it right back at them!
-Easy, easy.

23:13.750 --> 23:14.920
He's not the enemy.

23:15.090 --> 23:16.690
Don't you get it?

23:18.530 --> 23:20.030
We're nothing to them.

23:20.390 --> 23:23.830
Rats, snuck in from beyond the Wall.

23:24.870 --> 23:26.730
Sure, they had a use for us...

23:26.870 --> 23:29.000
...when they realized
we could work their magic.

23:29.140 --> 23:31.940
So they handpicked us
from all the other rats out there...

23:32.070 --> 23:36.910
...and just let us nibble away
at his royal majesty's precious power.

23:37.610 --> 23:39.710
But as soon as this war's all over...

23:39.980 --> 23:42.180
...it's back to the sewers for all of us.

23:43.120 --> 23:46.450
That means you too, hero.

23:46.620 --> 23:52.430
You missing home so much, Libertus,
why don't you and Nyx head on back?

23:52.560 --> 23:54.900
I'm sure Niflheim will welcome you
with open arms.

23:55.130 --> 23:57.060
You've got a home out there too.

24:00.430 --> 24:01.770
Or did you forget?

24:09.740 --> 24:10.980
Damn it!

24:11.850 --> 24:13.780
I'm not gonna let it end like this.

24:20.020 --> 24:23.090
It is said sentiment amongst the people
is favorable, Your Majesty.

24:23.220 --> 24:25.630
Most all will welcome this peace.

24:25.790 --> 24:27.230
If you yourself
have not heard their voices...

24:27.560 --> 24:29.860
...how can you claim
to know their hearts?

24:30.700 --> 24:32.930
What of the mission to Tenebrae,
Your Majesty?

24:33.170 --> 24:35.500
Is such clandestine action wise?

24:35.740 --> 24:38.570
If discovered, it will only serve
to provoke the empire.

24:38.710 --> 24:41.840
The empire remains our enemy
until the treaty is signed.

24:42.040 --> 24:43.640
So long as we are at war...

24:43.780 --> 24:46.810
...His Majesty intends to remain
one step ahead of them.

24:47.180 --> 24:48.480
Of course.

24:59.630 --> 25:02.500
A hairpin? I didn't think you were
into that kind of thing.

25:02.660 --> 25:05.270
It's not for me.
It's a gift for the princess.

25:05.670 --> 25:07.870
But keep that quiet.
Nobody's supposed to know.

25:10.870 --> 25:12.140
Well, that's me.

25:13.170 --> 25:14.680
Watch your back out there.

25:15.240 --> 25:18.050
I know you're sick of hearing it,
but you're like a little--

25:18.180 --> 25:21.750
Little sister to you.
Yeah, I am sick of hearing it.

25:24.550 --> 25:27.020
Just make sure you come back
in one piece, all right?

25:30.990 --> 25:32.230
Says the guy in two pieces.

25:55.050 --> 25:57.820
Lady Lunafreya,
I have left the rear gate open.

25:57.950 --> 25:58.950
Thank you.

26:02.020 --> 26:03.060
Must you go?

26:03.190 --> 26:04.190
Yes.

26:06.860 --> 26:08.330
Then go quickly.

26:13.900 --> 26:17.140
I do not recall granting you permission to
leave your quarters, Lunafreya.

26:17.940 --> 26:19.140
Ravus.

26:23.740 --> 26:26.710
You are not to leave this room again
until the journey to Lucis.

26:26.850 --> 26:28.580
It is for your own good.

26:29.620 --> 26:30.850
My own good?

26:33.320 --> 26:35.160
What is truly going on here?

26:36.620 --> 26:39.590
What cause does the empire have
to see me wed to Noctis?

26:39.760 --> 26:43.030
They have offered a peace,
and your marriage is the olive branch.

26:43.300 --> 26:45.100
You expect me to believe that?

26:45.600 --> 26:47.270
What you believe does not concern me.

26:47.870 --> 26:49.970
What does concern me
is you sneaking off...

26:50.100 --> 26:53.170
...to go tell our mother's killer
about some plot you've dreamt up.

26:53.610 --> 26:55.880
You are wrong to hate King Regis.

26:56.680 --> 26:59.250
Niflheim killed Mother, not him.

27:00.650 --> 27:03.180
They murdered her
and made you their lapdog.

27:27.170 --> 27:28.410
It's done.

28:02.810 --> 28:07.250
<i>An air of jubilation has swept the city</i>
<i>in anticipation of the coming armistice.</i>

28:07.710 --> 28:11.990
<i>With only three days remaining until</i>
<i>the peace is officially signed into effect...</i>

28:12.150 --> 28:15.220
<i>...throngs of citizens</i>
<i>have taken to the streets to show....</i>

28:23.300 --> 28:25.870
<i>Lucis needs your strength,</i>
<i>young warriors.</i>

28:26.000 --> 28:27.300
<i>We don't need</i>
<i>any of you immigrants.</i>

28:28.800 --> 28:31.710
<i>Whatever strength you have</i>
<i>is on loan from the king.</i>

28:31.870 --> 28:35.110
<i>-You are nothing without him.</i>
<i>-Nyx, help Mother.</i>

28:35.280 --> 28:37.340
<i>Selena, get down.</i>

28:37.480 --> 28:40.750
<i>--and the waves of</i>
<i>imperial diplomats entering the city.</i>

28:42.320 --> 28:46.020
The princess? Are you certain?

28:46.150 --> 28:47.920
Yes, Your Majesty.

28:48.090 --> 28:52.290
She was amongst the last of
the imperial contingent to enter the city.

29:15.250 --> 29:16.520
Get in.

29:18.320 --> 29:21.090
I'm reporting to my post now though, sir.

29:21.290 --> 29:22.990
New orders.

29:23.120 --> 29:26.160
Come on.
We've got a princess to pick up.

29:33.230 --> 29:34.970
Nice ride, sir.

29:35.100 --> 29:37.270
It belongs to the prince.

29:37.400 --> 29:39.410
We've taken him outside the city.

29:39.540 --> 29:42.940
Doesn't he have a wedding to plan, sir?

29:43.810 --> 29:45.850
Cut the "sir" crap.

29:46.050 --> 29:48.020
The king has a plan of his own.

29:48.150 --> 29:51.520
Prince Noctis and Princess Lunafreya
are to meet far from Insomnia.

29:52.220 --> 29:53.250
What's she doing here then?

29:54.390 --> 29:56.820
Complicating things.

29:57.220 --> 30:00.090
We sent Crowe to find the princess
and escort her out of Tenebrae.

30:03.300 --> 30:06.270
We're still trying to figure out
what went wrong.

30:18.210 --> 30:24.080
So I know what you think about this war,
but what do you think about this peace?

30:26.450 --> 30:28.560
You happy giving up your home?

30:28.920 --> 30:31.560
It's the king's decision.
I owe him for taking me in.

30:32.230 --> 30:35.060
I was lucky.
There are people in Galahd who weren't.

30:36.030 --> 30:38.270
And they need me.

30:38.430 --> 30:40.570
So you're going back?

30:40.970 --> 30:43.400
What good will you be
without the king's magic?

30:47.140 --> 30:49.540
Yeah, always wanting to save somebody.

30:49.880 --> 30:52.350
I get it. Believe me.
But it doesn't win wars.

30:52.480 --> 30:54.980
It's not just wanting.

30:55.220 --> 30:57.280
It's not just me.

30:58.550 --> 31:00.590
Libertus is the one
you need to worry about.

31:00.920 --> 31:03.390
He'll go back if things gets worse.

31:05.890 --> 31:07.490
The worst is yet to come.

31:28.450 --> 31:30.620
Do you have any idea
who you're stopping?

31:30.950 --> 31:34.350
Open this gate now,
and maybe you'll have a job tomorrow.

31:34.990 --> 31:37.460
-King's orders.
-Are you sure you want to risk...

31:37.590 --> 31:40.390
...a diplomatic issue now, of all times?

31:40.530 --> 31:44.930
I am the personal escort
of Lady Lunafreya Nox Fleuret...

31:45.070 --> 31:47.430
...princess of the former Tenebrae and--

31:47.570 --> 31:50.470
And our kingdom's beloved bride-to-be.

31:50.600 --> 31:54.540
Welcome to sovereign jurisdiction.
We'll take care of things from here.

31:54.670 --> 31:57.240
-Forgive me, Captain Drautos.
-See Her Highness to the castle.

31:57.380 --> 32:00.450
I had no idea that you--
I wasn't made aware of any--

32:00.680 --> 32:02.680
-Excuse me. Thank you.
-No, you-- I must--

32:03.050 --> 32:05.020
I must-- No, I have to clear it
with my superiors first.

32:05.150 --> 32:06.590
Your Highness.

32:16.300 --> 32:21.200
Her Royal Highness,
Princess Lunafreya of Tenebrae.

32:28.640 --> 32:31.580
It has been a long time, Your Majesty.

32:32.610 --> 32:34.350
Yes.

32:35.050 --> 32:37.080
Far too long.

32:38.550 --> 32:41.460
Prince Noctis isn't here, is he?

32:42.160 --> 32:44.990
No, my dear. He is not.

32:48.030 --> 32:51.160
I am too old to fight this war.

32:51.300 --> 32:56.040
I have no choice but to receive the empire
and accept their treaty.

32:56.970 --> 32:58.000
Even so...

32:59.470 --> 33:03.140
...I had hoped to hold the wedding
elsewhere, somewhere safe.

33:03.280 --> 33:06.210
I sent one of my Glaive
to see you there, but--

33:09.180 --> 33:10.750
It is not too late.

33:11.590 --> 33:13.150
I can ready an escort.

33:13.290 --> 33:15.590
Please, go to my son.

33:17.690 --> 33:19.360
No.

33:20.560 --> 33:24.030
Wherever I go, the empire will follow.

33:24.660 --> 33:28.440
It would only place the prince
in greater danger.

33:29.340 --> 33:34.170
It is my duty to protect the prince
and see his destiny fulfilled.

33:34.310 --> 33:38.040
These 12 years
have not changed that.

33:39.150 --> 33:41.150
And what of your destiny?

33:41.750 --> 33:46.150
My duty is my destiny, Your Majesty.

33:46.620 --> 33:50.490
I'm prepared to accept
whatever may come to pass.

34:00.230 --> 34:01.370
So, what do you think?

34:01.770 --> 34:04.740
All these lands will be imperial soon.

34:05.070 --> 34:08.240
Reckon things will get better
when them Niffs start calling the shots?

34:08.380 --> 34:10.110
Not one damn bit.

34:10.240 --> 34:12.310
Don't matter who's calling the shots.

34:12.450 --> 34:14.380
Long as they're calling them
from behind the Wall...

34:14.510 --> 34:17.220
...ain't nothing gonna change
around here.

34:18.150 --> 34:19.390
Get over here.

34:19.520 --> 34:21.150
All right.

34:24.790 --> 34:26.490
<i>That's a hand!</i>

34:31.600 --> 34:33.600
I trust the reunion was a happy one?

34:33.730 --> 34:36.370
Has she been a hostage of Niflheim
all this time?

34:36.540 --> 34:38.610
She is a symbol of the peace.
That's all I'm told.

34:38.740 --> 34:39.740
Doesn't sound like it.

34:40.070 --> 34:41.840
Sounds like she's here
for something much bigger than that.

34:42.180 --> 34:44.280
Your orders are to protect her.

34:45.080 --> 34:47.550
Not to look, not to listen, not to think.

34:47.680 --> 34:49.420
Understood?

34:50.480 --> 34:51.620
Drautos.

34:51.750 --> 34:53.720
Yes, report.

34:59.460 --> 35:02.530
Get the hell out of my way.
That's my friend you got in there, damn it.

35:02.700 --> 35:04.630
Sir, you can't go in
until the examination has ended.

35:04.760 --> 35:06.770
What examination?
What the hell's going on?

35:07.100 --> 35:09.600
Hey, take it easy, big guy.

35:10.540 --> 35:13.740
These bastards rushed Crowe in there
the moment she got back.

35:13.870 --> 35:15.810
And now they won't let me in
to see her.

35:19.180 --> 35:20.580
Wait.

35:57.380 --> 35:59.690
Crowe's personal effects.

36:01.290 --> 36:03.160
Do with them as you see fit.

36:05.460 --> 36:08.660
So, what kind of mission
did you really send her on?

36:09.630 --> 36:13.600
No Glaive winds up dead
on a standard escort.

36:14.800 --> 36:18.610
I'll see the armistice does not interfere
with a full investigation.

36:21.170 --> 36:23.410
She was a good soldier.

36:23.740 --> 36:26.350
Her death will not go unanswered.

36:30.720 --> 36:32.750
What a life, huh?

36:35.490 --> 36:37.820
She was brought up an orphan.

36:38.560 --> 36:40.590
Run out of her village.

36:44.800 --> 36:47.700
I still remember the first time I saw her.

36:47.900 --> 36:49.900
Scrawny little thing...

36:50.240 --> 36:52.340
...all covered in dirt.

36:53.740 --> 36:55.910
Not a friend in the world.

36:59.380 --> 37:01.310
But those eyes....

37:01.480 --> 37:02.980
Damn.

37:03.350 --> 37:06.350
There was something
about those eyes.

37:14.290 --> 37:16.400
She deserved better.

37:17.500 --> 37:19.770
And I would've done anything
to give it to--

37:34.950 --> 37:37.550
Libertus, wait.

37:40.590 --> 37:41.860
Crowe died a Glaive.

37:42.020 --> 37:44.690
You can still honor her
by fighting as one.

37:46.430 --> 37:49.500
You're dumber than me sometimes,
you know that?

37:49.630 --> 37:51.560
Don't you get it?

37:51.800 --> 37:54.370
Lucis killed Crowe.

38:00.570 --> 38:02.610
Go back to the castle.

38:02.740 --> 38:07.980
Tell the king there's no peace to be had
from throwing the weak to the wolves.

38:08.720 --> 38:11.820
I'll fight my own fight from here on out.

38:13.650 --> 38:17.290
See you around, hero.

38:46.350 --> 38:47.490
<i>A hairpin?</i>

38:47.620 --> 38:49.520
<i>I didn't think you were</i>
<i>into that kind of thing.</i>

38:49.690 --> 38:51.890
<i>It's not for me.</i>
<i>It's a gift for the princess.</i>

39:31.000 --> 39:34.430
A most grand reception, King Regis.

39:34.970 --> 39:36.970
You honor all of Niflheim.

39:37.100 --> 39:41.040
Oh, the honor is ours,
Emperor Aldercapt.

39:41.410 --> 39:44.680
You have ventured far
to grace us with your presence.

39:45.550 --> 39:47.880
It was the very least I could do.

39:49.720 --> 39:53.790
Tomorrow will be an historic day
for both our nations.

39:54.050 --> 39:58.160
And your Insomnia is truly a marvel.

39:59.390 --> 40:02.630
My own cities pale in comparison.

40:03.760 --> 40:07.770
I pray we are able to take away much
from this visit.

40:14.870 --> 40:16.410
Hello.

40:18.580 --> 40:21.080
I am afraid we were never
properly introduced yesterday.

40:22.880 --> 40:26.490
I'm afraid it's going to have to wait,
Your Highness. I'm on guard duty.

40:26.850 --> 40:29.190
Then surely there's
no safer place for me to be.

40:31.720 --> 40:33.590
May I ask your name?

40:35.190 --> 40:38.130
Nyx. Nyx Ulric.

40:39.470 --> 40:43.040
There is something else
I wish to ask you, Nyx Ulric.

40:44.040 --> 40:46.770
King Regis said he sent
one of your order to come find me.

40:48.540 --> 40:51.480
I should like to offer my thanks in person.

40:51.780 --> 40:54.480
Where might I find this brave soldier?

41:02.090 --> 41:03.790
Oh, I did not--

41:03.960 --> 41:06.130
-I am so sorry.
-Don't be.

41:09.660 --> 41:10.700
Here.

41:13.000 --> 41:15.070
She was carrying this.

41:16.040 --> 41:17.140
It was meant for you.

41:19.170 --> 41:20.770
For me?

41:21.640 --> 41:22.880
Keep it.

41:23.580 --> 41:25.710
She would've wanted you to have it.

41:28.780 --> 41:31.180
I will carry it with me always.

41:31.620 --> 41:33.050
Thank you.

42:02.750 --> 42:05.720
Do you have any idea
what this peace means?

42:05.950 --> 42:08.220
It means our homes are gone...

42:08.550 --> 42:09.860
...all of them...

42:09.990 --> 42:11.760
...forever.

42:16.200 --> 42:18.260
Heard I could find
some treaty haters here.

42:18.870 --> 42:21.000
I come to the right place?

42:21.130 --> 42:22.900
You certainly have.

42:23.040 --> 42:25.270
Everyone say hello to a man
who spends his days...

42:25.610 --> 42:27.670
...in the loyal service of our good king.

42:27.810 --> 42:29.680
"Spent."

42:30.140 --> 42:32.150
Those days are over.

42:32.950 --> 42:35.310
I'm done listening
to that bastard's lies.

42:35.650 --> 42:38.180
He may sit on a throne,
but he ain't no king...

42:38.320 --> 42:40.590
...least not of mine.

42:40.950 --> 42:42.690
Well, then...

42:43.190 --> 42:45.930
...welcome to the resistance, brother.

42:46.730 --> 42:48.660
I hope you're here to talk.

42:49.060 --> 42:50.600
What do you wanna know?

43:00.240 --> 43:01.840
Please...

43:01.970 --> 43:04.580
...wherever Noctis is, keep him safe.

43:04.910 --> 43:06.680
That is all I ask.

43:06.810 --> 43:08.950
To what god do you pray?

43:09.120 --> 43:12.850
You, the slave of fate and destiny.

43:14.290 --> 43:16.690
Abandon your prayers.

43:16.860 --> 43:18.620
The gods do not listen.

43:18.760 --> 43:21.730
General Glauca. Why are you here?

43:21.890 --> 43:25.830
You are far too clever
to have ever believed in this peace.

43:26.330 --> 43:30.040
Pity you couldn't see your beloved Noctis.
You have another purpose.

43:30.170 --> 43:32.940
-I'm not here for Niflheim.
-No.

43:33.070 --> 43:34.340
You are here for me.

43:34.810 --> 43:35.810
You?

43:35.940 --> 43:37.280
I do not understand.

43:37.610 --> 43:40.150
Come tomorrow, you will.

44:28.360 --> 44:30.360
<i>Niflheim contingent has left the hotel.</i>

44:30.700 --> 44:32.830
<i>Less than three hours</i>
<i>until the ceremony.</i>

44:33.030 --> 44:34.700
<i>Bolster the Citadel guard.</i>

44:41.910 --> 44:43.710
<i>Nyx, is the princess with you?</i>

44:43.880 --> 44:44.880
No.

44:45.010 --> 44:46.350
I'm on duty at the Citadel.

44:46.910 --> 44:49.020
<i>Well, the Niffs just left</i>
<i>for the ceremony.</i>

44:49.150 --> 44:51.180
<i>And she wasn't with them.</i>

45:13.270 --> 45:15.740
<i>-A homing beacon?</i>
-Yeah, I'll send the coordinates now.

45:15.880 --> 45:17.240
Can you pinpoint a location for me?

45:17.380 --> 45:19.780
<i>Sure, but it sounds like</i>
<i>a wild-goose chase.</i>

45:19.910 --> 45:21.710
<i>Guess you got some</i>
<i>free time on your hands, huh?</i>

45:21.850 --> 45:24.780
Guess I do, for better or worse.

45:48.110 --> 45:50.510
<i>Those coordinates are about</i>
<i>20 miles south of Insomnia.</i>

45:51.010 --> 45:52.450
Outside the Wall.

45:52.810 --> 45:55.380
<i>What the hell was Crowe doing</i>
<i>all the way out there?</i>

45:55.820 --> 45:57.750
No, no. They sent her to--

46:00.920 --> 46:02.190
I need another favor, Pelna.

46:02.320 --> 46:04.260
Pull those coordinates up on the radar
and let me know what you find.

46:04.390 --> 46:07.190
<i>On it. You're thinking</i>
<i>this is all a big deal now, huh?</i>

46:07.360 --> 46:08.460
Yeah, too big to ignore.

46:11.760 --> 46:13.870
-Excuse me, sir. Excuse me.
-Hey, hey, hey.

46:14.000 --> 46:15.940
-Whoa, wait a minute.
-Stop right there.

46:20.770 --> 46:23.480
Listen up. This is not the gate watch.

46:23.810 --> 46:27.780
This is the heart of our city,
the home of our king.

46:27.910 --> 46:30.450
The ceremony must not be disturbed.

46:30.780 --> 46:34.050
Neutralize any threat quickly and quietly.

46:34.390 --> 46:35.920
Is that understood?

46:36.060 --> 46:37.890
Yes, sir.

47:23.470 --> 47:25.400
Glaive to command.
Are you there, captain?

47:25.540 --> 47:27.110
Urgent.

47:28.140 --> 47:29.940
Damn it, Drautos.

47:30.940 --> 47:34.050
<i>Jackpot, Nyx. There's a whole fleet of</i>
<i>airships sitting at that spot.</i>

47:34.180 --> 47:36.180
-Niflheim.
<i>-Yup, and from the looks of it...</i>

47:36.320 --> 47:37.950
<i>...I'd say they're headed to war.</i>

47:38.120 --> 47:39.390
-Where's the captain?
<i>-Should be at the Citadel.</i>

47:39.520 --> 47:40.950
There's no answer on his frequency.

47:41.090 --> 47:43.260
<i>I don't know, must have his hands full</i>
<i>with the escort detail.</i>

47:43.420 --> 47:47.060
Pelna, one last favor.
I need you to prep the Glaive for action.

47:47.190 --> 47:48.330
<i>What are you talking about?</i>

47:48.460 --> 47:50.230
<i>You wanna deploy</i>
<i>without the captain's order?</i>

47:50.400 --> 47:51.630
Trust me. Just get it done.

47:51.960 --> 47:53.530
<i>Wait, what am I supposed to tell--?</i>

47:53.900 --> 47:54.930
Stand down, Glaive.

48:00.540 --> 48:02.640
The ceremony is in less than two hours.

48:02.980 --> 48:04.880
We must make ready.

48:07.310 --> 48:09.050
Very well.

48:09.280 --> 48:10.420
Your Majesty.

48:10.580 --> 48:12.450
A man of the Kingsglaive is here, sire.

48:12.590 --> 48:14.090
He demands an audience.

48:14.290 --> 48:15.620
"Demands"?

48:16.220 --> 48:17.360
-Your Majesty, please.
-Halt.

48:17.660 --> 48:19.460
Give the order to deploy the Glaive.

48:22.430 --> 48:23.660
You.

48:24.030 --> 48:26.630
A Niflheim fleet makes ready for war
20 miles to the south.

48:26.970 --> 48:28.570
An imperial fleet.

48:28.970 --> 48:30.240
And they have the princess.

48:32.170 --> 48:35.240
Clarus, post guards
outside the treaty room.

48:35.370 --> 48:37.280
It will be seen
as a lack of faith in the peace.

48:37.410 --> 48:39.110
Which we all harbor.

48:39.480 --> 48:41.280
See it done.

48:41.580 --> 48:44.080
We may well have to take
Emperor Aldercapt into custody.

48:44.350 --> 48:45.990
Detain him?

48:46.120 --> 48:48.350
That would go beyond
a new declaration of war.

48:48.490 --> 48:51.020
We are still at war, Clarus.

48:52.220 --> 48:55.360
And you, Nyx Ulric.

48:55.930 --> 48:57.960
How soon can the Kingsglaive deploy?

48:59.300 --> 49:01.470
On your word, at once.

49:02.100 --> 49:03.600
Go, then.

49:04.070 --> 49:05.370
Save Luna.

49:10.580 --> 49:12.340
What if this is a diversion?

49:12.510 --> 49:13.710
Not likely.

49:14.050 --> 49:16.220
Tenebrae's princess is onboard.

49:21.650 --> 49:23.260
We've got two jobs.

49:24.320 --> 49:25.560
Save her.

49:26.260 --> 49:29.260
And stop those Niff ships
from flying on Insomnia.

49:36.240 --> 49:38.070
We go in teams.

49:38.670 --> 49:41.610
Standard infiltrate and extract.

49:42.310 --> 49:44.510
Nyx, you command. We'll follow.

49:47.650 --> 49:51.220
The Glaive stands together,
captain or no.

49:51.380 --> 49:52.420
For hearth.

49:52.550 --> 49:54.150
And home!

50:06.430 --> 50:11.440
<i>We are less than 20 minutes away</i>
<i>from the signing of this historic treaty.</i>

50:20.180 --> 50:22.150
<i>I received word</i>
<i>of the king's order to deploy.</i>

50:22.280 --> 50:23.680
<i>I'll see to matters in the city.</i>

50:24.750 --> 50:27.750
<i>You have your mission,</i>
<i>and it won't be easy.</i>

50:28.090 --> 50:29.420
<i>The objective is two-fold.</i>

50:29.560 --> 50:31.760
<i>Secure the hostage,</i>
<i>and stay the enemy advance.</i>

50:32.160 --> 50:34.190
<i>Just be careful.</i>

50:34.330 --> 50:36.600
<i>One Glaive already died</i>
<i>for this princess.</i>

50:36.760 --> 50:39.400
<i>Niflheim won't give her up easily.</i>

50:52.680 --> 50:53.750
<i>Team Two.</i>

51:13.170 --> 51:14.370
<i>Oh, man.</i>

51:14.530 --> 51:16.240
<i>Hurry up, Nyx!</i>

51:23.340 --> 51:24.740
<i>Help!</i>

51:38.860 --> 51:40.490
Over here.

51:42.260 --> 51:43.700
Preparing to head below deck.

51:43.830 --> 51:46.570
<i>Do not engage the enemy</i>
<i>until instructed.</i>

51:46.700 --> 51:48.230
<i>The ceremony is underway.</i>

51:48.370 --> 51:51.170
<i>Let's wait and see</i>
<i>how Niflheim plays this.</i>

51:56.280 --> 51:58.310
The Kingsglaive
have infiltrated the ships.

51:58.440 --> 52:00.750
So everything's going according to plan.

52:28.710 --> 52:34.210
Ulric reporting. Six Niflheim airships
confirmed inbound for Insomnia.

52:38.750 --> 52:42.790
Nyx, this doesn't feel like a war fleet.

53:06.810 --> 53:09.780
I think I might've found her.
I got a guarded door here.

53:09.920 --> 53:12.920
<i>Two Niff MTs. What's the plan?</i>

53:15.620 --> 53:17.520
Hold position.

53:17.690 --> 53:21.530
Arrived at destination.
High possibility of target in the vicinity.

53:24.260 --> 53:26.430
<i>Proceed to secure.</i>

53:26.630 --> 53:27.900
It's going to mean a fight.

53:28.270 --> 53:30.740
<i>Keep it quiet and keep it confined.</i>

53:30.870 --> 53:33.940
Pelna, you're clear to engage.
But keep it quiet.

53:34.310 --> 53:35.940
I'm on my way.

53:41.580 --> 53:43.250
Forgive my delay.

53:43.380 --> 53:45.620
A bit of unforeseen trouble.

53:45.750 --> 53:48.620
Nothing too vexing, I hope.

53:48.920 --> 53:51.590
A simple theft, nothing more.

53:51.720 --> 53:53.960
A daring thief, to steal from the king.

53:54.830 --> 54:00.570
Perhaps magical walls and castle gates
do not keep all things safe.

54:00.700 --> 54:02.330
Perhaps.

54:02.700 --> 54:06.570
But no matter. That which was taken
will soon be returned.

54:06.710 --> 54:08.570
Impressive.

54:08.770 --> 54:12.880
You are a paragon of kingly composure.

54:14.480 --> 54:16.620
But I must ask...

54:16.820 --> 54:19.520
...how can you be so sure?

54:20.250 --> 54:22.890
Because this thing is no mere trinket.

54:23.020 --> 54:25.890
It possesses a will all its own.

54:26.390 --> 54:29.390
Enough to break any thief's grasp.

54:31.530 --> 54:36.440
That sounds a very fine prize indeed.

54:44.940 --> 54:47.650
Not now, damn it.

54:49.350 --> 54:51.420
For me? You shouldn't have.

54:55.050 --> 54:57.620
Target confirmed. She's unharmed.

55:02.760 --> 55:06.330
The Glaives have recovered the princess,
Your Majesty.

55:09.870 --> 55:12.300
<i>Have you found your thief?</i>

55:12.470 --> 55:13.770
We have.

55:13.910 --> 55:16.580
And what was stolen remains intact.

55:16.710 --> 55:18.040
Joyous news.

55:18.380 --> 55:20.750
I am relieved to hear it.

55:21.680 --> 55:23.350
Tell me...

55:23.620 --> 55:24.850
...how heavy a sentence...

55:24.980 --> 55:27.990
...does the crime of theft
carry in your empire?

55:28.350 --> 55:29.620
Among the heaviest.

55:29.760 --> 55:32.020
Although there is one...

55:32.760 --> 55:33.930
...exception.

55:34.930 --> 55:37.400
Things are about to get ugly over here.

55:39.460 --> 55:41.570
Pelna, get out of there. It's a trap.

55:42.400 --> 55:44.740
-What is that?
-A curious old law...

55:44.870 --> 55:47.570
...I still permit in the outlands.

55:47.710 --> 55:50.610
A thief who escapes his captor...

55:50.740 --> 55:53.410
...can no longer be held to account
for his crime.

55:54.880 --> 55:56.880
A warning to the victim.

55:57.050 --> 56:01.490
Never show weakness,
lest you forgo the hand of justice.

56:01.650 --> 56:03.860
Oh, no, good king.

56:04.920 --> 56:06.930
Far from it.

56:07.390 --> 56:09.130
<i>The treaty is now on the table.</i>

56:09.460 --> 56:11.930
<i>The countdown begins</i>
<i>to this historical moment.</i>

56:12.060 --> 56:16.370
<i>It is a warning</i>
<i>to the hand of justice itself...</i>

56:16.840 --> 56:20.070
...never to loose its grip.

56:32.820 --> 56:34.720
Unit One, secure the perimeter.

56:34.850 --> 56:36.720
Unit Two, stand your ground.

56:38.560 --> 56:40.030
Pelna.

56:40.160 --> 56:43.630
One Tenebrae princess, safe and--

56:46.430 --> 56:47.430
Come on.

57:12.460 --> 57:15.030
The crystal. They're after the crystal.

57:20.170 --> 57:22.630
There's something going on below deck.

57:23.000 --> 57:25.600
The ship's not going to make it
to Insom--

57:32.010 --> 57:33.710
You....

57:35.950 --> 57:37.450
<i>What's going on?</i>

57:37.580 --> 57:38.750
<i>Insomnia is under attack.</i>

57:39.650 --> 57:41.550
Who brought you here?

57:41.890 --> 57:43.990
-General Glauca.
-You were bait.

57:44.120 --> 57:46.490
Us coming here was all part of their plan.

58:13.620 --> 58:16.960
Target secured.
Request permission to withdraw.

58:19.730 --> 58:20.760
<i>Granted. Get to--</i>

58:46.220 --> 58:48.620
The crystal will not serve you.

58:48.790 --> 58:50.760
Nor you...

58:50.960 --> 58:53.960
...once I take it from this accursed city.

58:54.790 --> 58:57.530
It's not the crystal I'm here for.

58:57.860 --> 58:59.930
The Wall. It's gone.

59:03.040 --> 59:04.240
Fall back. It's a trap.

59:12.580 --> 59:14.610
What the hell is going on?

59:25.320 --> 59:26.930
Traitors.

59:27.830 --> 59:29.760
What's got into you?

01:02:15.960 --> 01:02:18.300
Come, we must escape while we can.

01:02:18.430 --> 01:02:20.170
No, Clarus.

01:02:21.400 --> 01:02:23.870
I fear escape is no longer an option.

01:02:31.740 --> 01:02:33.880
General Glauca.

01:02:38.820 --> 01:02:40.950
Can you make it up? Can you stand?

01:03:02.340 --> 01:03:03.910
Luche!

01:03:11.020 --> 01:03:12.850
What are you doing?

01:03:20.960 --> 01:03:22.960
You gotta be kidding me.

01:03:28.800 --> 01:03:31.170
They teach piloting
back at the royal academy?

01:03:31.300 --> 01:03:33.100
Give me that.

01:03:38.010 --> 01:03:40.510
Been a long time
since I fought at your side, old friend.

01:03:40.850 --> 01:03:42.150
Yes...

01:03:42.350 --> 01:03:45.150
...but this time it is not your fight.

01:03:45.280 --> 01:03:47.050
If you wish to leave, go now.

01:03:47.190 --> 01:03:50.390
And abandon my king? I think not.

01:03:50.520 --> 01:03:54.090
Besides, our magic is bound to you.

01:03:54.530 --> 01:03:57.000
If you fall, Lucis falls.

01:03:57.860 --> 01:04:00.100
Then let us once more into the fray...

01:04:00.230 --> 01:04:01.900
...old friend.

01:04:28.490 --> 01:04:30.630
You must take me back to King Regis.

01:04:30.960 --> 01:04:33.530
Are you out of your mind?
Insomnia's a war zone.

01:04:34.130 --> 01:04:36.530
I have a duty. I cannot neglect it.

01:04:36.870 --> 01:04:40.110
-Yeah, I heard all that before.
-Then you know we must hurry.

01:04:40.240 --> 01:04:42.140
Hurry to do what? Get yourself killed?

01:04:42.270 --> 01:04:43.270
I do not fear death.

01:04:43.410 --> 01:04:46.310
Enough with all this brave princess act.

01:04:50.220 --> 01:04:52.920
Just pray this thing will make the trip.

01:05:17.440 --> 01:05:18.980
Clarus.

01:05:22.610 --> 01:05:27.020
Well, I daresay everything has proceeded
according to plan.

01:05:27.490 --> 01:05:29.420
-No?
-So it has.

01:05:29.550 --> 01:05:31.290
We have broken the Wall.

01:05:31.420 --> 01:05:34.060
All that remains is to break the city.

01:05:36.030 --> 01:05:38.260
Shall we take our leave, then?

01:05:38.400 --> 01:05:40.430
The sun will soon set.

01:05:40.600 --> 01:05:45.170
We need not be here
to witness the terrors of the night.

01:05:57.280 --> 01:05:58.380
The crystal.

01:06:02.350 --> 01:06:05.060
You're going too fast.
We have to land.

01:06:05.190 --> 01:06:09.160
-You're gonna have to give me a minute.
-There is no time. I will go on my own.

01:06:09.290 --> 01:06:12.360
You got wings underneath that dress?
You can't use magic.

01:06:13.630 --> 01:06:15.530
Not all miracles are made by magic.

01:06:15.670 --> 01:06:17.440
I do not fear death.

01:06:17.570 --> 01:06:20.510
What I fear is doing nothing
and losing everything.

01:06:22.740 --> 01:06:24.010
Oh, come on.

01:06:31.080 --> 01:06:34.520
You can thank magic for that miracle,
Your Highness.

01:06:55.140 --> 01:06:56.370
The reckoning is at hand.

01:07:00.680 --> 01:07:02.480
Dawn of a new age.

01:07:06.650 --> 01:07:10.050
You have the crystal.
What more would you take from me?

01:07:24.400 --> 01:07:26.640
The Ring of the Lucii.

01:07:27.240 --> 01:07:30.240
<i>I lost my mother, my country,</i>
<i>my birth-right.</i>

01:07:30.380 --> 01:07:32.710
Niflheim was the only life left to me.

01:07:33.580 --> 01:07:35.580
But all of that was for this.

01:07:37.780 --> 01:07:39.350
The ring belongs to me now.

01:07:48.730 --> 01:07:53.630
Hear me, Lucian kings of old,
for I am Ravus Nox Fleuret...

01:07:53.800 --> 01:07:57.270
...and none is more worthy of your power
than I.

01:07:58.100 --> 01:08:01.370
No. Why?

01:08:01.510 --> 01:08:03.510
Why do you refuse me?

01:08:24.600 --> 01:08:26.130
Look out.

01:08:51.690 --> 01:08:53.320
Quickly, through here.

01:09:13.480 --> 01:09:15.580
This leads to a hidden passageway.

01:09:15.710 --> 01:09:16.750
Follow it.

01:09:16.880 --> 01:09:18.650
Once you are away, make for Altissia.

01:09:18.780 --> 01:09:20.180
Noctis awaits you there.

01:09:20.890 --> 01:09:23.250
-Your Majesty.
-You knew this was coming--

01:09:23.390 --> 01:09:26.390
Yes. But it was the only way
to draw their wrath from Noctis.

01:09:27.930 --> 01:09:30.290
Is that the way of our king?

01:09:30.430 --> 01:09:33.600
Sacrifice Lucian sons to save his own?

01:09:33.730 --> 01:09:35.470
To save the world.

01:09:37.900 --> 01:09:39.670
See Luna safely to Altissia.

01:09:41.710 --> 01:09:44.410
This is not an order
from a king to his Glaive.

01:09:44.540 --> 01:09:47.950
This is a plea from one man to another.
Please, Nyx Ulric, keep her safe.

01:09:49.280 --> 01:09:50.820
For the future of all.

01:09:50.950 --> 01:09:52.780
The future?

01:09:55.790 --> 01:09:57.490
Here.

01:09:57.720 --> 01:09:58.960
Take this.

01:09:59.290 --> 01:10:02.730
It is time it passed to another's keeping.

01:10:34.330 --> 01:10:37.360
No, please. Stop.

01:10:37.600 --> 01:10:39.430
-Get back.
-Please. Don't leave us.

01:10:41.500 --> 01:10:44.440
I know your mother
would wish the same as me.

01:10:44.800 --> 01:10:48.440
That you and Noctis live happily.

01:10:48.570 --> 01:10:51.580
All those years captive
because I failed you.

01:10:51.710 --> 01:10:52.740
Not again.

01:10:52.880 --> 01:10:55.780
Locked doors
will seal your fate no longer.

01:10:55.910 --> 01:10:57.850
King Regis....

01:10:59.580 --> 01:11:02.750
Our hope goes with you now,
Nyx Ulric. Godspeed.

01:11:39.020 --> 01:11:40.730
Behold the King of Lucis...

01:11:41.730 --> 01:11:44.530
...who hoarded tranquility
within his precious walls.

01:11:45.400 --> 01:11:48.530
Where is your tranquility now, king?

01:11:49.470 --> 01:11:53.600
Here is your peace,
by steel's swift descent.

01:12:09.520 --> 01:12:11.060
Go.

01:12:31.040 --> 01:12:34.580
No. We must get away from here.

01:12:35.680 --> 01:12:37.550
It is what your king wanted.

01:13:18.390 --> 01:13:20.060
<i>Lady Lunafreya has escaped</i>
<i>with the ring.</i>

01:13:20.760 --> 01:13:21.830
<i>Find her at once.</i>

01:13:21.960 --> 01:13:23.530
<i>She is not to leave the city.</i>

01:13:25.800 --> 01:13:28.630
-Ulric to command. Come in, captain.
<i>-Footage of the perpetrators...</i>

01:13:28.770 --> 01:13:30.770
<i>...was captured</i>
<i>by a nearby surveillance camera.</i>

01:13:30.900 --> 01:13:32.870
<i>Here are images of the six suspects.</i>

01:13:33.800 --> 01:13:36.910
<i>One has been identified</i>
<i>as Galahdian refugee, Libertus Ostium...</i>

01:13:37.040 --> 01:13:40.540
<i>...a former member</i>
<i>of the Lucian Kingsglaive.</i>

01:13:42.580 --> 01:13:44.480
Hey, come here. Come here.

01:13:44.620 --> 01:13:46.620
I got you, I got you. You're all right.

01:13:46.750 --> 01:13:48.490
You're okay.

01:13:49.090 --> 01:13:50.620
It's fine.

01:13:50.760 --> 01:13:51.960
We're free.

01:13:52.560 --> 01:13:53.930
We're free now.

01:13:54.060 --> 01:13:56.030
We're free? What do you mean,
"We're free"?

01:13:56.160 --> 01:13:58.830
The empire. They promised.

01:13:59.930 --> 01:14:01.670
This district's ours.

01:14:02.000 --> 01:14:03.600
All the refugees.

01:14:03.730 --> 01:14:05.600
It's our new home.

01:14:06.100 --> 01:14:09.210
-The empire? You went in with Niflheim?
-Here.

01:14:10.170 --> 01:14:12.640
Take this. Meet up with the others.

01:14:14.580 --> 01:14:17.720
You're the hero of our revolution, brother.

01:14:22.820 --> 01:14:23.850
Damn it.

01:14:32.460 --> 01:14:35.100
This guy just doesn't know
when he's beat.

01:14:35.800 --> 01:14:38.670
-Can you drive?
-I can try.

01:14:42.170 --> 01:14:43.640
I'll be right back.

01:14:54.720 --> 01:14:57.090
No warping for you this time, hero.

01:15:01.830 --> 01:15:03.960
Give me the wheel. Go.

01:15:06.730 --> 01:15:08.030
You are without your magic.

01:15:08.170 --> 01:15:11.900
You noticed that, huh?
It must have died with the king.

01:15:12.200 --> 01:15:16.270
You're making a mess of my city, Glaive.
I thought I told you not to go playing hero.

01:15:17.010 --> 01:15:18.140
Leave the ship to me.

01:15:18.780 --> 01:15:21.050
Looks like you got a royal fare to see to.

01:16:10.730 --> 01:16:11.960
Move it.

01:16:37.250 --> 01:16:40.020
Maybe not all miracles
are made by magic.

01:16:49.130 --> 01:16:50.730
Oh, great.

01:17:08.850 --> 01:17:10.890
The hell did you do
to piss these things off?

01:17:11.020 --> 01:17:13.820
It's not me they're after.
It's the ring.

01:17:13.960 --> 01:17:17.330
What's so special about this ring?
Don't tell me the future's riding on it.

01:17:17.660 --> 01:17:19.300
He who wears the ring
communes with the Lucii...

01:17:19.630 --> 01:17:21.900
-...and commands great power.
-What kind of power?

01:17:22.030 --> 01:17:24.940
A forbidden one.
Sealed within the ring, long ago.

01:17:25.700 --> 01:17:30.010
The Old Wall.
I thought that was just a bedtime story.

01:17:37.720 --> 01:17:39.080
I can assure you it is not.

01:17:39.220 --> 01:17:42.320
But the Lucii grant their power
only to those they deem worthy.

01:17:42.650 --> 01:17:44.760
So that guy who tried it on back there...

01:17:44.890 --> 01:17:46.760
...I guess he wasn't deemed worthy.

01:17:48.230 --> 01:17:49.430
That was my brother.

01:17:52.300 --> 01:17:54.430
These 12 years have changed Ravus.

01:17:54.800 --> 01:17:57.700
He is bound by the past,
and lost in his lust for power.

01:17:59.800 --> 01:18:01.140
How the hell did they find us?

01:18:21.030 --> 01:18:23.390
Your hairpin. They're tracking it.
Give it to me.

01:18:31.140 --> 01:18:35.240
I had a little sister once.
She was killed when the empire came.

01:18:37.110 --> 01:18:38.940
I couldn't save her.

01:18:39.840 --> 01:18:42.850
I was as helpless then as I am now.

01:18:45.280 --> 01:18:48.020
I couldn't show her the future
she wanted.

01:18:50.150 --> 01:18:54.160
True power is not something that is found
by those who seek it.

01:18:55.230 --> 01:18:57.860
It is something that comes
to those who deserve it.

01:19:00.500 --> 01:19:02.900
Your sister wanted you to see
a future as well.

01:19:05.970 --> 01:19:08.910
Anyone would wish the same
for family they love.

01:19:13.080 --> 01:19:15.780
You don't pull any punches, do you?

01:19:23.490 --> 01:19:24.990
I'm over here.

01:19:25.320 --> 01:19:27.390
<i>Do you hear me?</i>
<i>Repeat, this is Drautos.</i>

01:19:27.520 --> 01:19:28.990
<i>Can you hear me? Over.</i>

01:19:29.230 --> 01:19:31.260
Your timing's impeccable, captain.

01:19:36.830 --> 01:19:38.340
If the Lucii are real...

01:19:38.470 --> 01:19:41.340
...they sure don't seem to mind
their city getting torn apart.

01:19:47.340 --> 01:19:49.450
<i>You're to rendezvous and regroup.</i>
<i>Understood?</i>

01:19:52.020 --> 01:19:53.380
Might not be so easy, captain.

01:19:54.920 --> 01:19:57.050
My wings have been clipped,
if you didn't know.

01:20:29.350 --> 01:20:31.090
<i>Ulric. Are you all right?</i>

01:20:32.590 --> 01:20:34.590
I'm not dead, if that's what you mean, sir.

01:20:35.430 --> 01:20:37.560
<i>Head for Section D</i>
<i>as soon as you can.</i>

01:20:37.900 --> 01:20:40.130
<i>I'll have an evacuation team ready.</i>

01:20:40.530 --> 01:20:43.130
Don't suppose you could meet me
at the gate.

01:20:43.270 --> 01:20:45.540
I'd kind of like to
get the hell out of this city.

01:20:45.870 --> 01:20:48.410
<i>Imperials hold all exits.</i>
<i>There's no way through.</i>

01:20:48.540 --> 01:20:49.940
<i>I'll meet you at Section D.</i>

01:20:50.070 --> 01:20:54.110
<i>Cut all radio contact until then.</i>
<i>And make sure you get there.</i>

01:20:54.240 --> 01:20:55.280
It's a date, sir.

01:21:12.100 --> 01:21:14.400
Ain't no turning back now.

01:21:14.530 --> 01:21:15.970
<i>Status report.</i>

01:21:16.100 --> 01:21:18.100
<i>Ulric killed some good men.</i>

01:21:18.240 --> 01:21:20.400
<i>-What about the ring?</i>
<i>-We don't have it yet.</i>

01:21:21.870 --> 01:21:24.070
<i>This is Glauca. King Regis is dead.</i>

01:21:24.270 --> 01:21:26.880
<i>The ring is on its way to Section D.</i>

01:21:27.010 --> 01:21:29.450
<i>We must recover the ring</i>
<i>to realize our goal.</i>

01:21:29.580 --> 01:21:32.450
<i>If Ulric or the princess get in the way,</i>
<i>take them out.</i>

01:21:32.580 --> 01:21:35.020
<i>Reclaim our hearth and home.</i>

01:21:35.150 --> 01:21:37.090
"Hearth and home"?

01:21:37.220 --> 01:21:38.320
<i>Libertus, come in.</i>

01:21:38.460 --> 01:21:40.190
<i>Where are you? Are you all right?</i>

01:21:40.320 --> 01:21:41.590
I'm fine.

01:21:42.490 --> 01:21:44.400
On the way back to base now.

01:21:44.530 --> 01:21:47.100
<i>We need you to head to the junction</i>
<i>in Section D.</i>

01:21:47.230 --> 01:21:50.400
<i>We're gonna join with another unit,</i>
<i>make a clean sweep of the place.</i>

01:21:50.530 --> 01:21:53.240
<i>We're one step away</i>
<i>from realizing this revolution.</i>

01:21:53.370 --> 01:21:55.540
<i>Let's not let Pruvia's death be in vain.</i>

01:21:55.670 --> 01:21:58.080
<i>We'll be waiting for you, hero.</i>

01:22:25.000 --> 01:22:27.940
-Don't move until I say it's safe, all right?
-I won't.

01:22:36.280 --> 01:22:38.080
Ulric, reporting.

01:22:39.280 --> 01:22:41.350
I have the princess.

01:22:41.490 --> 01:22:43.550
She's alive and well.

01:22:51.460 --> 01:22:52.730
-No!
-Get out of here.

01:22:56.100 --> 01:22:58.500
You've got some fight in you, Nyx,
I'll give you that.

01:23:00.470 --> 01:23:02.170
Run. Now.

01:23:04.010 --> 01:23:08.180
I can't believe you're still moving
with that hollowpoint in you.

01:23:08.310 --> 01:23:12.050
All Crowe could do was scream,
when one tore her insides apart.

01:23:13.350 --> 01:23:17.150
-Why'd you do it?
-Because the Kingsglaive is nothing.

01:23:17.290 --> 01:23:18.760
An old man's battle fodder...

01:23:19.090 --> 01:23:20.690
...sent to die in Insomnia's war...

01:23:21.020 --> 01:23:22.630
...while our homes
are bound and shackled.

01:23:23.630 --> 01:23:25.530
Niflheim took your home.

01:23:27.760 --> 01:23:29.630
Took all our homes!

01:23:30.670 --> 01:23:32.600
Nothing will ever change that.

01:23:33.040 --> 01:23:34.770
You never were too smart.

01:23:36.510 --> 01:23:39.240
You could've had a new future
with the empire.

01:23:56.390 --> 01:23:59.300
There's nowhere to run, princess.

01:23:59.700 --> 01:24:00.700
The ring.

01:24:03.070 --> 01:24:04.500
Give it to me.

01:24:27.720 --> 01:24:29.660
So many dead over so simple a thing.

01:24:30.790 --> 01:24:34.130
But why? For what?

01:24:34.570 --> 01:24:36.300
Power.

01:24:36.500 --> 01:24:39.170
Untold power,
beyond the control of someone like you.

01:25:22.880 --> 01:25:24.620
Captain.

01:25:37.630 --> 01:25:39.200
Nyx.

01:25:41.600 --> 01:25:45.300
It's over. The daemons are unleashed.

01:25:46.300 --> 01:25:48.740
Lucis is fallen.

01:25:50.910 --> 01:25:52.380
Surrender the ring.

01:25:56.380 --> 01:25:58.920
Plan on giving those kings
a piece of your mind, princess?

01:26:00.720 --> 01:26:03.750
You got a destiny to take care of here,
remember?

01:26:04.290 --> 01:26:07.360
Besides, didn't anyone tell you?

01:26:10.360 --> 01:26:11.700
I'm the hero around here.

01:26:29.410 --> 01:26:33.850
Show yourselves, kings of Lucis.

01:26:38.460 --> 01:26:41.590
You call upon the wards
of this world's future, mortal.

01:26:41.730 --> 01:26:46.530
And if you come lusting for our power,
you must first stand in our judgment.

01:26:46.830 --> 01:26:51.540
How long will you do nothing
whilst Insomnia burns?

01:26:51.900 --> 01:26:54.400
Old or new, or whatever it is.

01:26:55.470 --> 01:26:57.570
Summon your Wall.

01:26:58.310 --> 01:26:59.780
You do not command us.

01:26:59.910 --> 01:27:03.250
Yours is not even royal blood.

01:27:03.380 --> 01:27:06.450
It does not fall to us to guard your city.

01:27:06.580 --> 01:27:07.950
Man is a fool creature...

01:27:08.290 --> 01:27:11.320
...clinging to his past
and cowering from his future.

01:27:11.460 --> 01:27:14.930
Wasting his strength on bygone days.

01:27:15.460 --> 01:27:18.260
And what future are you wards of?

01:27:18.400 --> 01:27:19.660
So shortsighted.

01:27:19.800 --> 01:27:22.270
And cursed never to rise above it.

01:27:22.430 --> 01:27:23.530
Wait.

01:27:23.670 --> 01:27:26.940
I have seen what this brave soul
is prepared to do.

01:27:27.270 --> 01:27:29.870
He, too, seeks to safeguard the future.

01:27:30.010 --> 01:27:31.410
Your Majesty.

01:27:32.010 --> 01:27:35.880
Very well, young king.
We will weigh your warrior's worth.

01:27:36.250 --> 01:27:38.650
But our boon does not come cheap.

01:27:38.950 --> 01:27:44.960
The cost is a life. His or hers.

01:27:45.420 --> 01:27:46.820
No.

01:27:48.460 --> 01:27:50.590
To hell with your power.

01:27:51.830 --> 01:27:53.860
I'm not here for it.

01:27:55.400 --> 01:27:59.540
I only came to tell you, you are no kings.

01:28:00.270 --> 01:28:02.970
Your worth has been weighed
and found wanting.

01:28:03.340 --> 01:28:04.910
Now burn.

01:28:11.310 --> 01:28:13.880
You're going to lose your precious ring.

01:28:16.720 --> 01:28:19.520
But it's not too late to save it.

01:28:20.420 --> 01:28:22.430
You mean to barter for your life.

01:28:22.560 --> 01:28:24.530
No, no.

01:28:25.560 --> 01:28:27.660
My life is nothing.

01:28:30.070 --> 01:28:33.570
Giving a future
to those who want to see it...

01:28:35.310 --> 01:28:36.910
...is everything.

01:28:38.910 --> 01:28:42.450
You do not fear,
even if that future is doomed.

01:28:42.580 --> 01:28:46.650
If that sentiment is not false,
perhaps you are worthy.

01:28:47.080 --> 01:28:49.620
We will grant you our light.

01:28:49.750 --> 01:28:52.690
But know it will set when the sun rises.

01:28:53.320 --> 01:28:56.560
And the price for it will be your life.

01:28:58.760 --> 01:29:01.730
You guys drive a hard bargain.

01:29:04.470 --> 01:29:06.400
<i>Where do I sign?</i>

01:29:16.380 --> 01:29:18.550
I could get used to this.

01:29:24.020 --> 01:29:25.020
Nyx....

01:29:26.420 --> 01:29:27.990
-I'm sorry.
-Don't be.

01:29:29.360 --> 01:29:30.860
You saved me.

01:29:31.530 --> 01:29:32.860
Now I owe you.

01:29:33.030 --> 01:29:34.730
For a change.

01:29:35.830 --> 01:29:37.370
I'm gonna need another favor.

01:29:37.500 --> 01:29:41.670
Meet Lunafreya Nox Fleuret,
our prince's beloved bride-to-be.

01:29:41.810 --> 01:29:44.740
And she has the future of the world
in her hands.

01:29:44.870 --> 01:29:48.380
Keep her safe, get her out of Insomnia.

01:29:48.950 --> 01:29:51.410
Oh, I almost forgot. You'll need this.

01:29:53.420 --> 01:29:56.120
Give Prince Noctis my regards.

01:29:56.890 --> 01:29:58.960
Libertus will take care of you from here.

01:29:59.120 --> 01:30:02.430
Have a safe journey, Your Highness.

01:30:02.860 --> 01:30:05.760
-What will come of you?
-What the hell are you doing?

01:30:06.430 --> 01:30:08.400
Following the kings' orders.

01:30:09.030 --> 01:30:11.640
I will see the ring to Noctis.

01:30:12.870 --> 01:30:15.140
The future will be safe. I swear it.

01:30:25.480 --> 01:30:28.420
Planning on punching your way
out of the city? Keep it.

01:30:28.950 --> 01:30:30.820
-Now we're even.
-No.

01:30:31.120 --> 01:30:33.620
We'll settle up
once you're back in Galahd.

01:30:33.790 --> 01:30:36.190
Me and everyone else
will be waiting for you.

01:30:36.560 --> 01:30:37.860
I'm counting on you...

01:30:39.130 --> 01:30:40.160
...hero.

01:30:59.020 --> 01:31:02.190
-Buckle up, princess.
-My life is in your hands.

01:31:12.030 --> 01:31:15.530
So, the power of the Lucii returns.

01:31:15.930 --> 01:31:17.670
No matter. You are out of time.

01:31:17.800 --> 01:31:19.870
For you, I'll make some.

01:31:53.700 --> 01:31:56.010
What can you hope to do?

01:31:57.610 --> 01:32:00.540
One man against an empire.

01:32:00.680 --> 01:32:02.510
Against the daemons.

01:32:02.750 --> 01:32:06.720
How will you save Insomnia
with no wall to protect you?

01:32:08.180 --> 01:32:12.190
You've got it all wrong.
I'm not fighting to save Insomnia.

01:33:38.240 --> 01:33:43.280
So this is the might of the Old Wall.

01:33:43.650 --> 01:33:47.180
Marvelous. Truly marvelous.

01:34:58.250 --> 01:35:00.260
Why'd you do it?

01:35:00.690 --> 01:35:02.930
Lucis. Niflheim.

01:35:03.060 --> 01:35:05.800
It isn't who we fight for that matters,
only what.

01:35:06.730 --> 01:35:10.830
We fight for our homes.
That is where our allegiance lies.

01:36:30.210 --> 01:36:32.550
That's not something you see every day.

01:36:48.970 --> 01:36:52.200
Oh, such a pitiable waste.

01:36:52.340 --> 01:36:57.140
All those beautiful city streets,
all laid to unsightly ruin.

01:36:57.310 --> 01:37:00.810
-I will return to Niflheim.
-So soon?

01:37:01.410 --> 01:37:03.080
The crystal is ours.

01:37:03.980 --> 01:37:05.150
Finish this...

01:37:05.420 --> 01:37:07.980
...and see the daemons disposed of.

01:37:08.120 --> 01:37:09.420
As you command.

01:37:11.290 --> 01:37:13.820
Such a pitiable waste.

01:37:27.100 --> 01:37:29.540
How could you serve the empire?

01:37:30.140 --> 01:37:32.980
After everything they did?

01:37:33.510 --> 01:37:37.110
I do not fault them
for taking what was given.

01:37:39.220 --> 01:37:41.880
I fault the man who gave it.

01:37:42.390 --> 01:37:44.350
The man who cowered behind his wall...

01:37:44.520 --> 01:37:48.390
...and abandoned us
to save his throne and his son.

01:37:49.090 --> 01:37:52.100
Give me the ring,
and our homes will be free again.

01:37:52.230 --> 01:37:54.460
The empire has promised it.

01:37:55.230 --> 01:37:59.140
I don't see much of a future
on the other side of that promise.

01:37:59.300 --> 01:38:00.940
Don't be a fool.

01:38:01.070 --> 01:38:02.570
Save your friends.

01:38:04.140 --> 01:38:05.910
Give your dead sister peace.

01:38:07.010 --> 01:38:09.650
What do you fight for if not that?

01:38:55.060 --> 01:38:57.430
Hang on. This could get bumpy.

01:39:07.200 --> 01:39:08.700
Drautos.

01:39:17.180 --> 01:39:18.650
Here, take the wheel.

01:39:27.120 --> 01:39:28.690
Floor it!

01:39:39.140 --> 01:39:41.600
-Libertus!
-Just keep your foot on the gas.

01:40:02.360 --> 01:40:04.060
You're all right?

01:40:10.330 --> 01:40:12.470
I'll be waiting for you, hero.

01:40:39.800 --> 01:40:41.500
What of your kings' power now?

01:40:41.630 --> 01:40:45.400
They've given you a burden
you cannot hope to bear.

01:40:46.800 --> 01:40:48.570
I told you before.

01:40:48.740 --> 01:40:52.140
Just wanting doesn't win wars.

01:42:04.610 --> 01:42:10.620
For the honor of my home,
I fought and killed under a king I loathed.

01:42:12.360 --> 01:42:14.720
And still he betrayed me.

01:42:16.160 --> 01:42:18.190
He betrayed us all.

01:42:18.330 --> 01:42:21.900
We fought for the same thing. All of us.

01:42:23.400 --> 01:42:25.400
But you've looked too long on the past.

01:42:26.370 --> 01:42:27.570
You're blind to the future.

01:42:32.640 --> 01:42:34.440
Predictable.

01:42:35.210 --> 01:42:38.810
Unlike you, I learn from history.

01:42:39.380 --> 01:42:42.150
But you're a slave to the past.

01:42:42.790 --> 01:42:45.590
A man's past is his pride.

01:42:46.320 --> 01:42:47.390
No.

01:42:47.690 --> 01:42:51.430
My pride is shaping the future.

01:43:03.940 --> 01:43:06.380
Looks like I'm gonna owe him big.

01:43:22.290 --> 01:43:23.890
We're almost there.

01:43:24.560 --> 01:43:25.730
Almost.

01:43:38.470 --> 01:43:41.640
King Regis did what he did for the future.

01:43:42.650 --> 01:43:44.580
Because of him...

01:43:45.450 --> 01:43:48.280
...there's still hope for our homes.

01:43:49.420 --> 01:43:51.250
Hope....

01:44:00.330 --> 01:44:02.530
Not the worst way to go.

01:44:03.270 --> 01:44:05.300
Rule well, young king.

01:44:25.690 --> 01:44:27.290
We should move.

01:44:29.260 --> 01:44:31.530
It ain't safe here either.

01:44:33.900 --> 01:44:35.400
Hey.

01:44:36.370 --> 01:44:38.370
Don't worry about Nyx.

01:44:39.600 --> 01:44:41.740
He can take care of himself.

01:44:46.840 --> 01:44:48.380
Come on.

01:44:50.580 --> 01:44:51.780
No.

01:44:54.550 --> 01:44:56.520
We must part ways here.

01:44:57.350 --> 01:44:58.590
What?

01:44:59.360 --> 01:45:02.890
I can hardly travel in secrecy
alongside so great a hero.

01:45:03.890 --> 01:45:07.000
And I, too, have a promise to keep to Nyx.

01:45:08.300 --> 01:45:10.630
I pray you two see each other again soon.

01:45:13.540 --> 01:45:14.970
Yeah.

01:45:16.870 --> 01:45:18.640
Me too.

01:45:21.480 --> 01:45:23.680
Thank you, Libertus.

01:45:41.460 --> 01:45:42.630
Hey, queen!

01:45:43.370 --> 01:45:46.670
You and the king
are always welcome in Galahd.

01:45:47.700 --> 01:45:50.440
Me and Nyx will be waiting for you.

01:54:47.080 --> 01:54:48.110
<i>It's been some while.</i>

01:54:48.240 --> 01:54:51.410
<i>Do you remember the last time</i>
<i>you saw Lady Lunafreya?</i>

01:54:52.080 --> 01:54:53.480
About 12 years ago.

01:54:53.620 --> 01:54:55.480
That would make you 8?

01:54:55.620 --> 01:54:58.190
-You were kids.
-Hope she hasn't gotten her hopes up.

01:54:58.320 --> 01:55:00.120
Why not? Calm yourself.

01:55:00.290 --> 01:55:02.260
Try and keep it together
when you meet her.

01:55:02.390 --> 01:55:05.230
-She'll expect to see a fine, young prince.
-Tell me something I don't know.

01:55:05.360 --> 01:55:07.560
We don't have time for all that.

01:55:07.900 --> 01:55:10.430
But this is your wedding
we're talking about, Noc.

01:55:10.570 --> 01:55:12.430
Knew that too.

01:55:12.570 --> 01:55:15.140
You really gotta calm down.

01:55:16.670 --> 01:55:19.210
What do you mean, "Uh-oh"?

01:55:19.340 --> 01:55:21.140
I think I know.
